        "original_id": "89694e22-c5e8-53d7-8f90-491544ed22ec",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Colin Newman, Graham Lewis, Bruce Gilbert, Robert Gotobed, Margaret Fiedler McGinnis, PJ Harvey\n- Bands: Wire, Young the Giant, Moonshake, Laika\n- Songs and Albums: \"Cough Syrup\", Young the Giant\n- Places: London, Irvine, California\n\nFacts:\n- Wire is an English rock band that was formed in London in October 1976.\n- Colin Newman, Graham Lewis, Bruce Gilbert, and Robert Gotobed formed Wire in October 1976.\n- Colin Newman was the vocalist and guitarist of Wire, Graham Lewis was the bassist and vocalist, Bruce Gilbert was the guitarist, and Robert Gotobed was the drummer.\n- Young the Giant is an American rock band that formed in Irvine, California, in 2004.\n- Margaret Fiedler McGinnis is best known as a founding member of the UK indie groups Moonshake and Laika.\n- Margaret Fiedler McGinnis also performed as a live guitarist with PJ Harvey and Wire.\n- \"Cough Syrup\" is a song by the American alternative rock band Young the Giant.\n- \"Cough Syrup\" appeared on Young the Giant's eponymous debut album.",
